}, "2": {"node_id": "54c6fa7c-c7c5-44dd-a7ba-5a12ebd20fb4", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {"file_path": "..\\data\\pg10763.txt", "file_name": "pg10763.txt", "file_type": "text/plain", "file_size": 405245, "creation_date": "2024-10-20", "last_modified_date": "2024-10-20"}, "hash": "b50ba5f8e93eef2a41343153cee41c103dee6090b5b5797de7f4b81e471b2fa2", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}, "3": {"node_id": "0cfd9a0b-336b-4eb2-89a4-81e0e899ca67", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "1ceab3a32fc0086dc261d2eb2ed8d080686e1b2599274117087912824edca92f", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "makes a man a man, whether born a serf or king;\r\n  And it's loaf, loaf, loaf, lolling on a bench or throne\r\n  That makes a being thewed to act a limp and useless thing!\r\n\r\n  No matter what you do, miracles or fruitless deeds,\r\n  You're a man, man, man, if you do them with a will;\r\n  And no matter how you loaf, cursing wealth or mumbling creeds,\r\n  You are nothing but a noise, and its weight is nil.\r\n\r\n  For it's be, be, be, champion of your heart and soul,\r\n  That makes a man a man, whether reared in silk or rags;\r\n  And it's talk, talk, talk, from a tattered shirt or stole,\r\n  That makes the image of a god a manikin that brags.\r\n\r\n\r\n_Richard Butler Glaenzer._\r\n\r\nFrom \"Munsey's Magazine.\"\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHAVING DONE AND DOING\r\n\r\n(ADAPTED FROM \"TROILUS AND CRESSIDA\")\r\n\r\n\r\nA member of Parliament, having succeeded notably in his maiden effort at\r\nspeech-making, remained silent through", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 90756, "end_char_idx": 91643, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "0cfd9a0b-336b-4eb2-89a4-81e0e899ca67", "embedding": [-0.014537806, 0.025495147, 0.0062630316, -0.00067111786, 0.005040062, 0.039698824, -0.040367793, 0.030971356, -0.008269668, 0.033438686, -0.0102998