ks,\r\n\r\n  \"For who would lose,\r\n  Though full of pain, this intellectual being,\r\n  These thoughts that wander through eternity,\r\n  To perish rather, swallowed up and lost\r\n  In the wide womb of uncreated night,\r\n  Devoid of sense and motion?\"\r\n\r\n\r\n  Praise the generous gods for giving\r\n    In a world of wrath and strife,\r\n  With a little time for living,\r\n    Unto all the joy of life.\r\n\r\n  At whatever source we drink it,\r\n    Art or love or faith or wine,\r\n  In whatever terms we think it,\r\n    It is common and divine.\r\n\r\n  Praise the high gods, for in giving\r\n    This to man, and this alone,\r\n  They have made his chance of living\r\n    Shine the equal of their own.\r\n\r\n\r\n_William Ernest Henley._\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nCOWARDS\r\n\r\n\r\nWe might as well accept the inevitable as the inevitable. There is no\r\nescaping death or taxes.\r\n\r\n\r\n  Cowards die many times before their deaths:\r\n  The valiant never", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 288304, "end_char_idx": 289292, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "7c2bf9e1-b518-4610-8908-5243c70dbae1", "embedding": [0.008653002, 0.033828095, 0.029996186, 0.003465143, 0.008843371, 0.0028928227, 0.0076271263, 0.02321775, 0.027348323, 0.038094964, -0.0003367859, -0.014490519, 0.04844753, 0.013555533, 0.019089377, -0.058427457, -0.025767725, 0.013545137, -0.091992185, 0.027525391, 0.07886034, 0.02356548, 0.017111776, -0.008339142, -0.020983603, 0.0068914215, 0.009901336, -0.034583453, 0.035413105, -0.0075642737, 0.043554854, 0.05766808, 0.04133757, -0.035196833, 0.054779638, 0.018642638, -0.026632953, 0.02416063, 0.05092664, -0.0076837474, -0.07942201, 0.03639727, -0.014422392, 0.047339097, -0.025541507, -0.020946583, -0.00849506, 0.0065079844, -0.0082683815, 0.05239377, 0.053084437, -0.007115792, -0.049286287, 0.01486540