da-b012-65761093a3b0", "node_type": "1", "metadata": {}, "hash": "89c0519ccd0b99b5f7dbab0a2be15e7b786ae4862b29980ad3601851b59682b4", "class_name": "RelatedNodeInfo"}}, "text": "Our lives are trailing the sordid dust.\r\n\r\n  We hope, we resolve, we aspire, we pray,\r\n    And we think that we mount the air on wings\r\n    Beyond the recall of sensual things,\r\n  While our feet still cling to the heavy clay.\r\n\r\n  Wings for the angels, but feet for men!\r\n    We may borrow the wings to find the way--\r\n    We may hope, and resolve, and aspire, and pray;\r\n  But our feet must rise, or we fall again.\r\n\r\n  Only in dreams is a ladder thrown\r\n    From the weary earth to the sapphire walls;\r\n    But the dreams depart, and the vision falls,\r\n  And the sleeper wakes on his pillow of stone.\r\n\r\n  Heaven is not reached at a single bound;\r\n    But we build the ladder by which we rise\r\n    From the lowly earth to the vaulted skies,\r\n  And we mount to its summit, round by round.\r\n\r\n\r\n_J.G. Holland._\r\n\r\nFrom \"Complete Poetical Writings.\"\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nRULES FOR THE ROAD\r\n\r\n\r\nArdor of sinew and spirit--what else do we", "mimetype": "text/plain", "start_char_idx": 297119, "end_char_idx": 298043, "text_template": "{metadata_str}\n\n{content}", "metadata_template": "{key}: {value}", "metadata_seperator": "\n", "class_name": "TextNode"}, "__type__": "1"}, {"__data__": {"id_": "c02c446b-9c7f-48da-b012-65761093a3b0", "embedding": [0.006616774, -0.0058886954, -0.02558429, 0.022717278, -0.030324435, 0.054238006, 0.011785388, 0.048176993, 0.026745792, 0.08064407, -0.028652554, 0.051346805, 0.07483614, 0.04062313, 0.073424295, -0.05130628, -0.031389054, -0.022892332, -0.06661133, 0.016388046, 0.028387355, -0.002490404, 0.038676806, -0.0037694417, -0.06047432, 0.01138499, 0.056109887, 0.009430423, 0.0025328414, -0.027729338, 0.0421602, 0.04419468, 0.040139515, -0.0055445456, 0.009798508, 0.023087513, -0.012431231, -0.005084739, 0.0021934893, -